is_error":false,"num_turns":24,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I added a rule to the network: a phase with no vehicles on any of its lanes can't be chosen or held while another phase has traffic. On the dev episodes the edited network scores 44.5 veh-h against the original's 44.7.\n\n- **What I changed and why:** the network is already efficient in normal traffic. When the 10 s minimum green ends, the current phase never has a halted vehicle left at its stop line. Its one flaw is that it favours the E-W through phase even when that phase is empty. In one recorded episode it held that empty green for about 30 minutes while 3 vehicles waited elsewhere, costing about 1.5 veh-h. I repurposed four first-layer units as \"this phase is empty\" detectors and four second-layer units as relays. Each relay lowers its phase's logit by 20 when the phase is empty. Probes on 40,000 synthetic states cut empty-phase choices from 2,960 to 0. Outside that rule, 37 recorded decisions (about 0.7%) changed as a side effect.\n- **Parameters changed:** 212 of 7,428.\n- **Simulator calls:** 3 of 10. The original scored 44.7 and both versions of the edit scored 44.5. No dev episode triggers the lock-up, so most of that 0.2 is noise. The real gain comes only in test episodes where the original would get stuck.\n- **Dev TTS of final weights:** 44.5 (low 34.8, nominal 44.6, high 54.0).\n- **Test predictions:** low 34.8, nominal 44.7, high 54.2.\n\nFiles are in `work/`:\n- `weights.npz`\n- `NOTES.md`\n- `predictions.json`","ttft_ms":1034,"type":"result","duration_ms":733391,"uuid":"e44b7f6d-10a0-404d-accb-b67856c75618","ttft_stream_ms":842,"time_to_request_ms":71,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":2,"system_prompt":6,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":9,"input_hooks":1,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":7,"tool_pool_refresh":17,"init_message":3,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":2,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"a